  "caption": "Quinn's footy debut: one big pivot on a planted foot, and a week later the ankle is still sore, higher up than a usual sprain. Stairs are the worst.\n\nThis can be a high ankle sprain, where the connection between the two shin bones above the ankle is strained. Each step loads it, so it often takes longer to settle than a classic rolled ankle.\n\nWhat often helps: an early assessment (stability shapes the plan), protecting it at first, then rebuilding movement, calf strength and balance before walking, jogging and cutting. Let push-off tolerance, not the calendar, guide you.\n\nIf you can't bear weight, or the sprain isn't settling as expected, get it checked promptly.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
